E63 draft — vilan-playground/todo onto the full-stack ladder (rung 2)
=====================================================================

A PROPOSAL, not an applied change. Nothing outside the vilan repository was
touched to produce it. Apply with:

    cd vilan-playground/todo && git apply /path/to/todo-app.patch

(or `patch -p1 < todo-app.patch` if that tree is not under git). Everything
above the first `diff --git` line is ignored by both.

WHAT MOVES

This is the app fullstack-dx.md §2.1 measured as the charter's own evidence:
19 counted lines, 10 of them ceremony. It goes to the top of the ladder,
because its shell is exactly what `Document::of` writes.

  - The three boot reads (`dist/client.js`, `dist/client.css`,
    `src/app.html`) become one `require_build("client")`. No path, no file
    name, no MIME type is spelled in this file any more.
  - The four-arm `match request.path()` becomes `.serve_build(build)`, which
    installs one route per artifact the build wrote — with the content type
    its extension implies, and with the chunk routes too if you ever set
    `split = true` on the client leg, with no further server edit.
  - `serve_service(port, protocol, fallback, on_ready)` becomes a
    `Server::builder()` chain the service is INSTALLED on
    (`.with_service(Service::new(protocol))`). Same routes, same wire; the
    difference is that the page and the service now compose instead of one
    owning the boot function. Delete the `.with_service(…)` line and the
    program still compiles and still serves the page.
  - `src/app.html` is DELETED, and `Document::of(build).title("Todo")` writes
    the page instead. The `<link>`, the `<script>` and the mount `<div id>`
    are all derived from the build, so they cannot disagree with the
    artifacts they name — which is the failure this whole arc exists to
    remove.

Counted by fullstack-dx.md §1.2's rule (non-blank, non-comment lines):
src/server.vl 19 → 20 lines, 10 → 6 ceremony, and src/app.html's 13 lines go
to zero. 32 lines across two files become 20 in one.

WHAT TO VERIFY WHEN YOU APPLY IT

1. The generated page against your `src/app.html`. They are semantically the
   same document and differ in four cosmetic ways — verified by fetching `/`
   from the migrated server on a scratch copy:

       -<!DOCTYPE html>            +<!doctype html>
       -\t<html lang="en">         +<html lang="en">      (your stray indent)
       -<meta charset="UTF-8">     +<meta charset="utf-8" />
       -…initial-scale=1.0">       +…initial-scale=1" />

   Nothing else moves: same title, same stylesheet link, same
   `<div id="app">`, same module `<script src="/client.js">`.

2. That you are happy losing the file. If you would rather keep it, drop the
   `src/app.html` hunk and swap one line —

       let page = require_shell("src/app.html", build).html();

   with `import std::document::require_shell;` in place of
   `import std::document::Document;`. That is rung 1 + rung 0+: your markup,
   still yours, and now CHECKED against the build at every boot (a `<link>`
   to a stylesheet the build no longer emits stops the server, naming the
   file and the fix, instead of serving an unstyled page that looks right).
   This is the rung the `vilan init` scaffold and the in-repo examples ship
   at, for the reason §6.3 gives.

3. The port and the greeting are unchanged (4600, "notes server listening
   on …"), and so is `Notes::new()` and everything in `src/store.vl`.

VERIFIED HERE

On a scratch copy of the whole app (it is small enough to copy whole):
`vilan build .` exits 0, `node dist/server.mjs` boots, `/` serves the
generated document above, `/client.js` answers `text/javascript`,
`/client.css` answers `text/css`. Checked with vilan 0.34.0.

NOT VERIFIED: the browser client actually running against it (no browser
here). Nothing in `src/store.vl` was touched — `Notes` is still the same
in-memory service it was.

